WEBVTT

00:01:30.002 --> 00:01:33.673
Now BCIs conjure up images
of science fiction like "The Matrix"

00:01:33.673 --> 00:01:37.051
with a cable jacked up into your brain
through a hole in your skull.

00:01:37.093 --> 00:01:41.430
But I'm here to show you that the future
can be much more elegant than that.

00:01:42.515 --> 00:01:44.392
So we got this group chat going,

00:01:44.433 --> 00:01:46.018
which I thought was a great idea,

00:01:46.018 --> 00:01:48.479
until they started roasting me
about the TED Talk --

00:01:48.521 --> 00:01:49.522
(Laughter)

00:01:49.522 --> 00:01:51.607
Which they found hilarious.

00:01:51.649 --> 00:01:53.568
Thanks for the vote of confidence, guys,

00:01:53.568 --> 00:01:54.944
bloody Australians.

00:01:54.944 --> 00:01:56.112
(Laughter)

00:01:56.112 --> 00:01:59.240
Now you can see it's still quite slow
for them to type this way,

00:01:59.282 --> 00:02:03.494
but this is like dial up speeds
at the beginning of the Internet.